=Research this topic thoroughly to build a full course curriculum:

TOPIC: {{ $json.topic }}
SKILL LEVEL: {{ $json.skill_level }}
AUDIENCE: {{ $json.audience }}

Find the core skills/subtopics a learner needs, common beginner mistakes, current best practices, useful tools, and concrete real-world examples. Make 5-8 targeted searches.

=Design a {{ $('⚙️ Prepare Context').item.json.module_count }}-module course.

TOPIC: {{ $('⚙️ Prepare Context').item.json.topic }}
SKILL LEVEL: {{ $('⚙️ Prepare Context').item.json.skill_level }}
AUDIENCE: {{ $('⚙️ Prepare Context').item.json.audience }}

RESEARCH TO GROUND THE CURRICULUM:
{{ $json.output }}

parameters.jsCode:
const cfg = $('⚙️ Prepare Context').first().json;
const raw = $input.first().json.output || '';
const match = raw.match(/```json\s*([\s\S]*?)```/i);
let modules = [];
if (match) {
  try { modules = JSON.parse(match[1]); } catch (e) { modules = []; }
}
if (!Array.isArray(modules) || modules.length === 0) {
  modules = [{ module_number: 1, module_title: cfg.topic, lessons: ['Overview of ' + cfg.topic] }];
}

return modules.map((m, i) => ({
  json: {
    topic: cfg.topic,
    skill_level: cfg.skill_level,
    audience: cfg.audience,
    instructor_voice: cfg.instructor_voice,
    module_number: m.module_number || (i + 1),
    module_title: m.module_title || `Module ${i + 1}`,
    lessons: m.lessons || []
  }
}));

parameters.text:
=Write full lesson content for Module {{ $json.module_number }}: {{ $json.module_title }} of the course "{{ $json.topic }}".

LESSONS TO COVER IN THIS MODULE:
{{ $json.lessons.join('\n- ') }}

AUDIENCE: {{ $json.audience }}
SKILL LEVEL: {{ $json.skill_level }}

RESEARCH TO DRAW FROM (cite facts inline as markdown links [Title](URL)):
{{ $('🔍 Research Agent').first().json.output }}

Write complete, ready-to-teach content for every lesson listed, each as its own "### Lesson: <title>" subsection, with clear explanations, at least one concrete example, and a short actionable exercise at the end of each lesson.

parameters.jsCode:
const cfg = $('⚙️ Prepare Context').first().json;
const research = $('🔍 Research Agent').first().json.output || '';
let sources = '_No structured sources returned — verify claims manually._';
const split = research.split(/###\s*SOURCES/i);
if (split.length > 1) sources = split[1].trim();

const humanizedItems = $input.all();
const outlineItems = $('🧩 Parse Course Outline').all();

const modules = humanizedItems.map((item, i) => {
  const outline = outlineItems[i] ? outlineItems[i].json : {};
  return {
    number: outline.module_number ?? (i + 1),
    title: outline.module_title ?? `Module ${i + 1}`,
    content: (item.json.output || '').trim()
  };
}).sort((a, b) => a.number - b.number);

const toc = modules.map(m => `- Module ${m.number}: ${m.title}`).join('\n');
const body = modules.map(m => `## Module ${m.number}: ${m.title}\n\n${m.content}`).join('\n\n---\n\n');

const date = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
const finalMarkdown = `# ${cfg.topic}\n\n*A ${cfg.skill_level} course for: ${cfg.audience}*\n*Generated: ${date}*\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n${toc}\n\n---\n\n${body}\n\n---\n\n## Sources & References\n\n${sources}\n`;

return [{
  json: {
    course_title: cfg.topic,
    skill_level: cfg.skill_level,
    module_count: modules.length,
    generated_date: date,
    final_markdown: finalMarkdown
  }
}];
